### Description

This Terraform program configures a Route 53 zone named "primary" and sets up a CloudWatch log group named "aws_route53_example_com" to capture query logs from the Route 53 zone. It also creates a CloudWatch log resource policy named "route53-query-logging-policy" to allow Route 53 to put log events into the specified CloudWatch log group.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "primary_zone" {
  name = "primary"
}

resource "aws_cloudwatch_log_group" "aws_route53_example_com_log_group" {
  name = "aws_route53_example_com"
}

resource "aws_cloudwatch_log_resource_policy" "route53_query_logging_policy" {
  policy_name = "route53-query-logging-policy"
  policy_document = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "route53.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action    = "logs:CreateLogStream"
        Resource  = "${aws_cloudwatch_log_group.aws_route53_example_com_log_group.arn}:*"
      },
      {
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "route53.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action    = "logs:PutLogEvents"
        Resource  = "${aws_cloudwatch_log_group.aws_route53_example_com_log_group.arn}:*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_route53_query_log" "primary_route53_query_log" {
  cloudwatch_log_group_arn = aws_cloudwatch_log_group.aws_route53_example_com_log_group.arn
  zone_id                  = aws_route53_zone.primary_zone.zone_id
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-east-1`. You can change this to any other region as needed.

2. **Route 53 Zone**: A Route 53 zone named "primary" is created.

3. **CloudWatch Log Group**: A CloudWatch log group named "aws_route53_example_com" is created to store the query logs.

4. **CloudWatch Log Resource Policy**: A CloudWatch log resource policy named "route53-query-logging-policy" is created to allow Route 53 to create log streams and put log events into the specified CloudWatch log group.

5. **Route 53 Query Log**: A Route 53 query log is configured to send query logs to the specified CloudWatch log group.

