### Description
This Terraform program creates two Elastic Beanstalk environments that share the same Elastic Beanstalk application. It also sets up an IAM role (`eb_ec2_role`) and an instance profile (`eb_ec2_profile`) required for the Elastic Beanstalk environments. The IAM role is configured with a basic assume role policy that allows EC2 to assume the role.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

# IAM Role for Elastic Beanstalk EC2 instances
resource "aws_iam_role" "eb_ec2_role" {
  name = "eb_ec2_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# IAM Instance Profile associated with the IAM Role
resource "aws_iam_instance_profile" "eb_ec2_profile" {
  name = "eb_ec2_profile"
  role = aws_iam_role.eb_ec2_role.name
}

# Elastic Beanstalk Application
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application" "my_application" {
  name = "my_application"
}

# First Elastic Beanstalk Environment
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "environment1" {
  application = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.my_application.name
  name        = "environment1"
  solution_stack_name = "64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.4.1 running Python 3.8"
  instance_profile = aws_iam_instance_profile.eb_ec2_profile.name
}

# Second Elastic Beanstalk Environment
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "environment2" {
  application = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.my_application.name
  name        = "environment2"
  solution_stack_name = "64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.4.1 running Python 3.8"
  instance_profile = aws_iam_instance_profile.eb_ec2_profile.name
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`. You can change this to any other region as per your requirement.
2. **IAM Role (`eb_ec2_role`)**: This role is created with a basic assume role policy that allows EC2 to assume the role.
3. **IAM Instance Profile (`eb_ec2_profile`)**: This instance profile is associated with the IAM role created above.
4. **Elastic Beanstalk Application (`my_application`)**: This is the Elastic Beanstalk application that will host the environments.
5. **Elastic Beanstalk Environments (`environment1` and `environment2`)**: Two environments are created under the same application, each using the same instance profile and solution stack.

