### Description
The Terraform program below creates an `aws_connect_bot_association` resource. This resource is used to associate an Amazon Lex bot with an AWS Connect instance. The configuration includes the required `instance_id` attribute and a nested `lex_bot` block that specifies the `name` of the Lex bot. The `lex_region` attribute is optional and can be specified if the Lex bot is in a different region than the AWS Connect instance.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"  # Default region, can be changed as needed
}

resource "aws_connect_bot_association" "connect_bot_association" {
  instance_id = "your-connect-instance-id"  # Replace with your actual Connect instance ID

  lex_bot {
    name       = "your-lex-bot-name"  # Replace with your actual Lex bot name
    lex_region = "us-west-2"         # Optional, specify if Lex bot is in a different region
  }
}
```

### Notes
- Replace `"your-connect-instance-id"` with the actual ID of your AWS Connect instance.
- Replace `"your-lex-bot-name"` with the actual name of your Amazon Lex bot.
- The `lex_region` attribute is optional and should be set if your Lex bot is located in a different AWS region than your Connect instance. If not specified, it defaults to the same region as the Connect instance.

