### Description
The Terraform program below creates an AWS Connect instance with SAML identity management and associates a Lex bot with it. The `aws_connect_instance` resource is configured with the necessary attributes, and the `aws_connect_bot_association` resource is linked to the instance using the `instance_id` obtained from the `aws_connect_instance` resource.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_connect_instance" "connect_instance_saml" {
  identity_management_type = "SAML"
  inbound_calls_enabled    = true
  outbound_calls_enabled   = true

  # Optional attributes
  instance_alias = "MyConnectInstance"
  tags = {
    Name = "MyConnectInstance"
  }
}

resource "aws_connect_bot_association" "connect_bot_association" {
  instance_id = aws_connect_instance.connect_instance_saml.id

  lex_bot {
    name = "MyLexBot"  # Replace with your Lex bot name
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration ensures that the AWS Connect instance is set up with SAML identity management and that a specified Lex bot is associated with it. Adjust the `instance_alias`, `tags`, and `lex_bot.name` as needed to fit your specific requirements.

