### Description
This Terraform program creates an Amazon Kendra data source with web crawler configuration, including URL exclusion and inclusion patterns. The program defines the necessary resources and configurations to set up the Kendra data source in a specified AWS region.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_kendra_data_source" "kendra_data_source" {
  index_id = "your-kendra-index-id"  # Replace with your actual Kendra index ID
  name     = "MyKendraDataSource"
  type     = "WEBCRAWLER"

  configuration {
    web_crawler_configuration {
      urls {
        seed_url_configuration {
          seed_urls = ["https://example.com"]  # Replace with your seed URLs
        }

        url_inclusion_patterns = ["https://example.com/included/*"]  # Replace with your inclusion patterns
        url_exclusion_patterns = ["https://example.com/excluded/*"]  # Replace with your exclusion patterns
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`. You can change this to your preferred region.
- **Kendra Data Source**: The `aws_kendra_data_source` resource is created with the following attributes:
  - `index_id`: The ID of the Kendra index where the data source will be associated. Replace `"your-kendra-index-id"` with your actual Kendra index ID.
  - `name`: The name of the Kendra data source.
  - `type`: The type of the data source, which is set to `WEBCRAWLER`.
- **Web Crawler Configuration**: Inside the `configuration` block, the `web_crawler_configuration` is defined with:
  - `urls`: Contains the seed URLs and URL patterns.
    - `seed_url_configuration`: Specifies the initial URLs to crawl.
    - `url_inclusion_patterns`: Defines the patterns for URLs to include in the crawling process.
    - `url_exclusion_patterns`: Defines the patterns for URLs to exclude from the crawling process.

Make sure to replace placeholders like `"your-kendra-index-id"`, seed URLs, and URL patterns with your actual values before deploying the Terraform configuration.

