### Description

This Terraform program creates an AWS SageMaker App configured as a JupyterServer. The program includes the necessary configuration for the `aws_sagemaker_app` resource, ensuring that all required attributes are specified. Additionally, it sets up an IAM role with the appropriate permissions to allow SageMaker to access other AWS services as required.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "domain_id" {
  description = "The ID of the SageMaker domain where the app will be created."
  type        = string
  default     = "example-domain-id"
}

variable "app_name" {
  description = "The name of the SageMaker app."
  type        = string
  default     = "jupyter-server-app"
}

variable "instance_type" {
  description = "The instance type for the SageMaker app."
  type        = string
  default     = "ml.t3.medium"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "sagemaker_role" {
  name = "sagemaker-jupyter-server-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "sagemaker.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "sagemaker_full_access" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSageMakerFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_role.name
}

resource "aws_sagemaker_app" "sagemaker_jupyter_server" {
  app_name       = var.app_name
  app_type       = "JupyterServer"
  domain_id      = var.domain_id
  user_profile_name = "default-user-profile"

  resource_spec {
    instance_type = var.instance_type
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **Variables**: 
   - `domain_id`: The ID of the SageMaker domain where the app will be created. Default value is `"example-domain-id"`.
   - `app_name`: The name of the SageMaker app. Default value is `"jupyter-server-app"`.
   - `instance_type`: The instance type for the SageMaker app. Default value is `"ml.t3.medium"`.
3. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `sagemaker-jupyter-server-role` is created with a trust policy allowing SageMaker to assume the role.
4. **IAM Role Policy Attachment**: The `AmazonSageMakerFullAccess` policy is attached to the IAM role to grant full access to SageMaker.
5. **SageMaker App**: A SageMaker app of type `JupyterServer` is created with the specified `app_name`, `app_type`, `domain_id`, and `user_profile_name`. The `resource_spec` block specifies the instance type for the app.

