### Description
The Terraform program defined below sets up the infrastructure for a video streaming site using AWS CloudFront and AWS S3. The program creates an S3 bucket to store the video content and a CloudFront distribution to distribute the content globally. The S3 bucket is configured with the necessary permissions to allow CloudFront to access the content.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "video_content_bucket" {
  bucket = "video-content-bucket-${random_string.bucket_suffix.result}"
  acl    = "private"

  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }

  lifecycle {
    create_before_destroy = true
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "VideoContentBucket"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "video_content_bucket_policy" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.video_content_bucket.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "cloudfront.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "s3:GetObject"
        Resource = "${aws_s3_bucket.video_content_bucket.arn}/*"
        Condition = {
          StringEquals = {
            "AWS:SourceArn" = "arn:aws:cloudfront::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:distribution/${aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_streaming_distribution.id}"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

data "aws_caller_identity" "current" {}

resource "aws_cloudfront_distribution" "video_streaming_distribution" {
  enabled = true

  origin {
    domain_name = "${aws_s3_bucket.video_content_bucket.bucket_regional_domain_name}"
    origin_id   = "S3Origin"
  }

  default_cache_behavior {
    allowed_methods  = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    cached_methods   = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    target_origin_id = "S3Origin"
    viewer_protocol_policy = "redirect-to-https"
  }

  restrictions {
    geo_restriction {
      restriction_type = "none"
    }
  }

  viewer_certificate {
    cloudfront_default_certificate = true
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "VideoStreamingDistribution"
  }
}

resource "random_string" "bucket_suffix" {
  length  = 8
  special = false
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **S3 Bucket**: An S3 bucket named `video-content-bucket-${random_string.bucket_suffix.result}` is created. The bucket is private and has versioning enabled.
3. **S3 Bucket Policy**: A bucket policy is attached to the S3 bucket to allow CloudFront to access the objects stored in the bucket.
4. **Caller Identity Data Source**: This data source retrieves the current AWS account ID.
5. **CloudFront Distribution**: A CloudFront distribution is created with the S3 bucket as the origin. The distribution is configured to redirect HTTP requests to HTTPS and has no geographic restrictions.
6. **Random String**: A random string is generated to ensure the S3 bucket name is unique.

