### Description of the Terraform Program

This Terraform program sets up the infrastructure for a video streaming site that distributes video content globally using AWS CloudFront, AWS Route53, and AWS S3. The program includes the following resources:

1. **AWS S3 Bucket (`aws_s3_bucket.video_content_bucket`)**: This bucket stores the video content that will be distributed via CloudFront.
2. **AWS CloudFront Distribution (`aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_streaming_distribution`)**: This distribution serves the video content from the S3 bucket globally.
3. **AWS Route53 Zone (`aws_route53_zone.video_streaming_zone`)**: This zone manages the DNS records for the video streaming domain.
4. **AWS Route53 Record (`aws_route53_record.video_streaming_record`)**: This record maps the domain name to the CloudFront distribution.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "video_content_bucket" {
  bucket = "video-content-bucket-${random_string.suffix.result}"
  acl    = "private"

  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }

  server_side_encryption_configuration {
    rule {
      apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {
        sse_algorithm = "AES256"
      }
    }
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "VideoContentBucket"
  }
}

resource "aws_cloudfront_distribution" "video_streaming_distribution" {
  enabled = true

  origin {
    domain_name = "${aws_s3_bucket.video_content_bucket.bucket_regional_domain_name}"
    origin_id   = "S3Origin"

    s3_origin_config {
      origin_access_identity = "origin-access-identity/cloudfront/E1234567890ABCDEF"
    }
  }

  default_cache_behavior {
    allowed_methods  = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    cached_methods   = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    target_origin_id = "S3Origin"
    viewer_protocol_policy = "redirect-to-https"

    forwarded_values {
      query_string = false
      cookies {
        forward = "none"
      }
    }
  }

  restrictions {
    geo_restriction {
      restriction_type = "none"
    }
  }

  viewer_certificate {
    cloudfront_default_certificate = true
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "VideoStreamingDistribution"
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "video_streaming_zone" {
  name = "video-streaming.com"
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "video_streaming_record" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.video_streaming_zone.zone_id
  name    = "www"
  type    = "A"

  alias {
    name                   = aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_streaming_distribution.domain_name
    zone_id                = aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_streaming_distribution.hosted_zone_id
    evaluate_target_health = true
  }
}

resource "random_string" "suffix" {
  length  = 8
  special = false
}
```

### Explanation

- **AWS S3 Bucket**: The bucket is created with versioning and server-side encryption enabled for data protection.
- **AWS CloudFront Distribution**: The distribution is configured to serve content from the S3 bucket. It uses the CloudFront default SSL certificate.
- **AWS Route53 Zone**: A Route53 zone is created for the domain `video-streaming.com`.
- **AWS Route53 Record**: An A record is created to map `www.video-streaming.com` to the CloudFront distribution.
- **Random String**: A random string is appended to the S3 bucket name to ensure uniqueness.

This setup ensures that the video content is globally distributed with high availability and security.

