LLM Output #0:
### Description
This Terraform program sets up a PostgreSQL 15 instance on AWS RDS within specific public subnets for running Airbyte connector test cases. The configuration includes managed settings for low maintenance, such as enabling auto-minor version upgrades and setting a backup retention period. The program assumes that the VPC, subnets, and security groups are already created and available.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

# Example VPC and Subnet IDs (replace with actual values)
variable "vpc_id" {
  type        = string
  description = "The ID of the VPC where the RDS instance will be deployed"
  default     = "vpc-12345678"
}

variable "subnet_ids" {
  type        = list(string)
  description = "List of subnet IDs where the RDS instance will be deployed"
  default     = ["subnet-12345678", "subnet-87654321"]
}

variable "security_group_id" {
  type        = string
  description = "The ID of the security group for the RDS instance"
  default     = "sg-12345678"
}

resource "aws_db_subnet_group" "airbyte_postgresql_subnet_group" {
  name       = "airbyte-postgresql-subnet-group"
  subnet_ids = var.subnet_ids

  tags = {
    Name = "AirbytePostgreSQLSubnetGroup"
  }
}

resource "aws_db_instance" "airbyte_postgresql_instance" {
  instance_class           = "db.t3.medium"  # Adjust instance class as needed
  allocated_storage        = 500
  engine                   = "postgres"
  engine_version           = "15"
  db_name                  = "airbyte_db"
  username                 = "airbyte_user"
  password                 = "secure_password"  # Replace with a secure password
  db_subnet_group_name     = aws_db_subnet_group.airbyte_postgresql_subnet_group.name
  vpc_security_group_ids   = [var.security_group_id]
  auto_minor_version_upgrade = true
  backup_retention_period  = 7

  timeouts {
    create = "30m"
    update = "30m"
    delete = "30m"
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "AirbytePostgreSQLInstance"
  }
}
```

### Notes
- **VPC and Subnet IDs**: Replace the placeholder values for `vpc_id`, `subnet_ids`, and `security_group_id` with actual values from your AWS environment.
- **Password**: Ensure the password is secure and follows best practices for database security.
- **Instance Class**: Adjust the `instance_class` based on your performance and cost requirements.
- **Region**: Set the desired AWS region in the `provider` block.

