This Terraform program sets up an AWS Lightsail Distribution with an EC2 instance as its origin. The program includes the necessary resources and configurations to ensure the distribution is correctly set up to serve content from the specified instance.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_instance" "instance" {
  ami           = "ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0"  # Example AMI ID for Amazon Linux 2
  instance_type = "t3.micro"

  tags = {
    Name = "lightsail-origin-instance"
  }
}

resource "aws_lightsail_distribution" "lightsail_distribution" {
  name       = "my-lightsail-distribution"
  bundle_id  = "small_1_0"
  is_enabled = true

  origin {
    name      = aws_instance.instance.id
    region_name = "us-west-2"
  }

  default_cache_behavior {
    behavior = "cache"
  }

  cache_behavior {
    path     = "/*"
    behavior = "cache"
  }

  cache_behavior_settings {
    allowed_http_methods = "GET,HEAD,OPTIONS,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE"
    cached_http_methods  = "GET,HEAD,OPTIONS"
    default_ttl          = 86400
    maximum_ttl          = 31536000
    minimum_ttl          = 0
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "my-lightsail-distribution"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **EC2 Instance**: An EC2 instance is created with a specified AMI and instance type. This instance serves as the origin for the Lightsail distribution.
3. **Lightsail Distribution**: A Lightsail distribution is created with the specified name and bundle ID. The distribution is enabled and configured to use the EC2 instance as its origin. Cache behaviors and settings are also configured to manage how content is cached and served.

This configuration ensures that the Lightsail distribution is correctly set up to serve content from the specified EC2 instance.

