### Description
This Terraform program creates an S3 Glacier vault, defines an IAM policy document for accessing the vault, and locks the vault using the defined policy. The program ensures that the Glacier vault lock depends on the existence of the Glacier vault and the IAM policy document.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_glacier_vault" "my_glacier_vault" {
  name = "my-glacier-vault"
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "glacier_access_policy" {
  statement {
    effect = "Allow"
    actions = [
      "glacier:InitiateJob",
      "glacier:GetJobOutput",
      "glacier:ListJobs",
      "glacier:DescribeVault",
      "glacier:UploadArchive",
      "glacier:InventoryRetrieval"
    ]
    resources = [
      "${aws_glacier_vault.my_glacier_vault.arn}"
    ]
  }
}

resource "aws_glacier_vault_lock" "my_glacier_vault_lock" {
  complete_lock = true
  policy      = data.aws_iam_policy_document.glacier_access_policy.json
  vault_name  = aws_glacier_vault.my_glacier_vault.name
}
```

This Terraform configuration does the following:
1. Configures the AWS provider with the region `us-west-2`.
2. Creates an S3 Glacier vault named `my-glacier-vault`.
3. Defines an IAM policy document that allows various Glacier operations on the vault.
4. Locks the Glacier vault using the defined policy document.

